COVERING CONNECTION: good rationals a/b <=> cluster residues {e mod b} leave a >2/7 run
<=> E FAILS to cover Z/b (at dilation a). So a good period exists <=> E under-covers some
small modulus b. For a COVERING-saturated S the reconstructed cluster is forced to
under-cover SOME small b (it cannot cover all of them with only k<=13 teeth) -- that
forced under-coverage is the good arc. Test: min over small b of the best empty-run:
  consec k=9 (k=9): under-covers (>2/7 run) at b=[13, 14]  => HAS good period
  perforated k=7 {0..8}\{1,7} (k=7): under-covers (>2/7 run) at b=[13, 14]  => HAS good period
  spread-21 k=11 (k=11): under-covers (>2/7 run) at b=[]  => NONE(!)
